00:03:24.536 --> 00:03:26.428
- Hey, Gary, Spiker Helms here.

00:03:26.428 --> 00:03:30.572
I was wondering, if you created
a social media platform,

00:03:30.572 --> 00:03:33.758
what would be your key feature and why?

00:03:33.758 --> 00:03:35.062
Can't wait to hear your response.

00:03:35.062 --> 00:03:35.764
See ya.

00:03:36.351 --> 00:03:37.065
- See ya!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.245
So, I've long had an idea,

00:03:40.245 --> 00:03:41.550
and I'm gonna share it with you guys,

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.551
which is the notion of a social network

00:03:44.551 --> 00:03:46.170
that looked like Instagram,

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.137
but more like Path, like you
could put any piece of content,

00:03:50.137 --> 00:03:52.642
could be a picture, a video, audio file,

00:03:52.642 --> 00:03:55.638
more content-agnostic so
not just picture or video,

00:03:55.638 --> 00:03:58.737
but also the ability to
do audio on top of that,

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:01.661
but the whole website, the whole app,

00:04:01.661 --> 00:04:05.207
the whole social network
was predicated on the notion

00:04:05.207 --> 00:04:08.683
that you can only speak
once a day in any 24 hours.

00:04:08.683 --> 00:04:10.517
So as soon as you put
out a piece of content,

00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:12.659
you would no longer be able to put out

00:04:12.659 --> 00:04:15.770
another piece of content
until 24 hours later,

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.074
because my belief is that the
supply and demand of noise

00:04:18.074 --> 00:04:20.146
is the real issue with social networks.

00:04:20.146 --> 00:04:22.365
Path went down how many people you follow.

00:04:22.365 --> 00:04:24.646
I think it's the amount
of pieces of content.

00:04:24.646 --> 00:04:26.333
I still think it's
gonna be a big business,

00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:29.799
I still think that restrictions
is where the action is

00:04:29.799 --> 00:04:32.191
for the short term, and
I would not be confused

00:04:32.191 --> 00:04:34.430
if we all look back at this video,

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:37.604
and talk about how I
predicted somebody going

00:04:37.604 --> 00:04:39.342
and executing this billion-dollar idea.

00:04:39.342 --> 00:04:41.826
I think the restriction of
one piece of content a day

00:04:41.826 --> 00:04:43.930
is where it's at, because
it forces all of us

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.136
as content providers, which all of us are,

00:04:46.136 --> 00:04:48.452
to put out the best
piece of quality content

00:04:48.452 --> 00:04:50.258
'cause it's that restriction, plus,

00:04:50.258 --> 00:04:51.145
there would be oomph behind it.

00:04:51.145 --> 00:04:53.112
Imagine I would say,
"Happy birthday, Alex,"

00:04:53.112 --> 00:04:55.126
and that was the only thing
I could say that day, wow!

00:04:55.126 --> 00:04:56.780
In a world where there's
so many other things

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:57.332
I want to put out,

00:04:57.332 --> 00:05:00.255
so my social network would be

00:05:00.255 --> 00:05:03.215
predicated on one piece of
content per person a day.

